<div class="component container col-12">
    <div class="component-content" >

    <div class="component footnotes col-12">
        <div class="component-content">
<div class="cf-footnotes">
    <h5>Footnotes</h5>
        <ol>
                    <li id="cf-fn-1">Douglass C. North, <em>Structure and Change in Economic History</em>, London, U.K.: W.W. Norton, 1981; Douglass C. North, <em>Institutions, Institutional Change, and Economic Performance</em>, Cambridge, U.K.: Cambridge University Press, 1990; and Douglass C. North,&nbsp;<a rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://ideas.repec.org/a/aea/jecper/v5y1991i1p97-112.html" class="offsite" target="_blank">&ldquo;Institutions,&rdquo;</a> <em>Journal of Economic Perspectives</em>&nbsp;5, 1991, pp. 97-112 (<a rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://ideas.repec.org/a/aea/jecper/v5y1991i1p97-112.html" class="offsite" target="_blank">https://ideas.repec.org/a/aea/jecper/v5y1991i1p97-112.html</a>).
                        <a href="#cf-fn-ret-1" aria-label="Return from footnote 1.">Return to 1</a>
                    </li>
                    <li id="cf-fn-2">Section 9C(2) of the U.K.&rsquo;s Financial Services Act 2012 says: &ldquo;The responsibility of the Committee in relation to the achievement by the Bank of the Financial Stability Objective relates primarily to the identification of, monitoring of, and taking of action to remove or reduce, system risks with a view to protecting and enhancing the resilience of the UK Financial System.&rdquo; See <a rel="noopener noreferrer" href="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/ukpga/2012/21/pdfs/ukpga_20120021_en.pdf" class="offsite" target="_blank">http://www.legislation.gov.uk/ukpga/2012/21/pdfs/ukpga_20120021_en.pdf</a>.
                        <a href="#cf-fn-ret-2" aria-label="Return from footnote 2.">Return to 2</a>
                    </li>
                    <li id="cf-fn-3">Section 9C(4) of the U.K.&rsquo;s Financial Services Act 2012 (<a rel="noopener noreferrer" href="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/ukpga/2012/21/pdfs/ukpga_20120021_en.pdf" class="offsite" target="_blank">http://www.legislation.gov.uk/ukpga/2012/21/pdfs/ukpga_20120021_en.pdf</a>).
                        <a href="#cf-fn-ret-3" aria-label="Return from footnote 3.">Return to 3</a>
                    </li>
                    <li id="cf-fn-4">Quantifying that tradeoff is difficult. Paul cites Romain Ranci&egrave;re, Aaron Tornell, and Frank Westermann, <a rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://ideas.repec.org/a/tpr/qjecon/v123y2008i1p359-406.html" target="_blank" class="offsite">&ldquo;Systemic Crises and Growth,&rdquo;</a> <em>Quarterly Journal of Economics</em> 123, February 2008, pp. 359-406 (<a rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://ideas.repec.org/a/tpr/qjecon/v123y2008i1p359-406.html" target="_blank" class="offsite">https://ideas.repec.org/a/tpr/qjecon/v123y2008i1p359-406.html</a>). Using a large group of countries, they find that average growth over 1960-2000 was higher in countries that have experienced occasional financial crises, as measured by the negative skewness of credit growth. They provide a model in which the enforceability of contracts plays an important role in engendering risk-taking and investment, which leads to higher growth.
                        <a href="#cf-fn-ret-4" aria-label="Return from footnote 4.">Return to 4</a>
                    </li>
                    <li id="cf-fn-5">For one of his early works, see Edward J. Kane, <a rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://ideas.repec.org/a/bla/jfinan/v36y1981i2p355-67.html" class="offsite" target="_blank">&ldquo;Accelerating Inflation, Technological Innovation, and the Decreasing Effectiveness of Banking Regulation,&rdquo;</a> <em>Journal of Finance</em>&nbsp;36, 1981, pp. 355-367 (<a rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://ideas.repec.org/a/bla/jfinan/v36y1981i2p355-67.html" target="_blank" class="offsite">https://ideas.repec.org/a/bla/jfinan/v36y1981i2p355-67.html</a>).
                        <a href="#cf-fn-ret-5" aria-label="Return from footnote 5.">Return to 5</a>
                    </li>
                    <li id="cf-fn-6">For a discussion, see John B. Taylor, <a rel="noopener noreferrer" href="http://object.cato.org/sites/cato.org/files/serials/files/cato-journal/2013/9/cjv33n3-2.pdf" target="_blank" class="offsite">&ldquo;Monetary Policy During the Past 30 Years with Lessons for the Next 30 Years,&rdquo;</a> luncheon address at the Cato Institute&rsquo;s 30th Annual Monetary Conference on Money, Markets and Government: The Next 30 Years, Washington D.C., November 15, 2012 (<a rel="noopener noreferrer" href="http://object.cato.org/sites/cato.org/files/serials/files/cato-journal/2013/9/cjv33n3-2.pdf" target="_blank" class="offsite">http://object.cato.org/sites/cato.org/files/serials/files/cato-journal/2013/9/cjv33n3-2.pdf</a>).
                        <a href="#cf-fn-ret-6" aria-label="Return from footnote 6.">Return to 6</a>
                    </li>
                    <li id="cf-fn-7">See Andrew G. Haldane and Vasileios Madouros, <a rel="noopener noreferrer" href="http://www.bis.org/review/r120905a.pdf" class="offsite" target="_blank">&ldquo;The Dog and the Frisbee,&rdquo;</a> speech at the Federal Reserve Bank of Kansas City&rsquo;s Economic Policy Symposium, &ldquo;The Changing Policy Landscape,&rdquo; Jackson Hole, WY, August 31, 2012 (<a rel="noopener noreferrer" href="http://www.bis.org/review/r120905a.pdf" class="offsite" target="_blank">http://www.bis.org/review/r120905a.pdf</a>).
                        <a href="#cf-fn-ret-7" aria-label="Return from footnote 7.">Return to 7</a>
                    </li>
                    <li id="cf-fn-8">See Sylvain Chassang, <a rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://ideas.repec.org/a/ecm/emetrp/v81y2013i5p1935-1971.html" class="offsite" target="_blank">&ldquo;Calibrated Incentive Contracts,&rdquo;</a> <em>Econometrica</em> 81, September 2013, pp. 1935-1971 (<a rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://ideas.repec.org/a/ecm/emetrp/v81y2013i5p1935-1971.html" target="_blank" class="offsite">https://ideas.repec.org/a/ecm/emetrp/v81y2013i5p1935-1971.html</a>).
                        <a href="#cf-fn-ret-8" aria-label="Return from footnote 8.">Return to 8</a>
                    </li>
                    <li id="cf-fn-9">See Luigi Zingales, <a rel="noopener noreferrer" href="http://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1111/jofi.12295/abstract" class="offsite" target="_blank">&ldquo;Does Finance Benefit Society?&rdquo;</a> <em>Journal of Finance</em> 70, August 2015, pp. 1327-1363 (<a rel="noopener noreferrer" href="http://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1111/jofi.12295/abstract" class="offsite" target="_blank">http://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1111/jofi.12295/abstract</a>). He cites the Chicago Booth-Kellogg School Financial Trust Index survey of a representative sample of about 1,000 American households, conducted by Social Science Research Solutions. Forty-eight percent of respondents to the December 2014 survey said that the U.S. financial system hurts the U.S. economy, while only 34 percent said it benefits the U.S. economy.
                        <a href="#cf-fn-ret-9" aria-label="Return from footnote 9.">Return to 9</a>
                    </li>
        </ol>
</div>
        </div>
    </div>
    </div>
</div>    <div class="component notes">
        <div class="component-content">

				
					
					
					
					
					
					

					  
						
						  
							
						
					
					
					 
						
							
											
					
					
					
						
					
					
							
						
					
				     
			
